{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.strong_channel_mirror_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.strong_channel_mirror_difference","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CrossingCountAffine.lean#L138-L143","doc":"And the strong channel is **not** mirror-invariant: its values differ by\n`4(Z - W)`. So the charge dependence the mirror splitting needs is present in\nthe model — in the wrong channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.coulomb_channel_mirror_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.coulomb_channel_mirror_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CrossingCountAffine.lean#L131-L136","doc":"**The mirror form.** The Coulomb channel takes the same value on `(Z, N)` and\non `(N, Z)`, so whatever coefficient multiplies it contributes **zero** to every\nmirror splitting. Stated at fixed `A`, which is what a mirror pair shares. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.no_crossing_combination_is_protonPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.no_crossing_combination_is_protonPairs","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CrossingCountAffine.lean#L116-L129","doc":"**No linear functional of the crossing counts is the proton-pair count.**\nOver `ℤ`, where `2 ≠ 0`. The quantifier order is the point: the coefficients\n`a, b, c` are chosen *first* and the contradiction follows for every choice, so\nthis excludes the whole family at once rather than one fit at a time. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.secondDiff_protonPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.secondDiff_protonPairs","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CrossingCountAffine.lean#L110-L112","doc":"**The second difference of `Z(Z-1)` is the constant `2`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.protonPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.protonPairs","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CrossingCountAffine.lean#L107-L108","doc":"The number of proton pairs, `Z(Z-1)` — what a Coulomb term must count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.secondDiff_crossing_combination_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.secondDiff_crossing_combination_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CrossingCountAffine.lean#L101-L105","doc":"**Every linear functional of the crossing counts is annihilated.** For any\ncoefficients `a b c` whatsoever, and at any fixed `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.secondDiff_affine_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.secondDiff_affine_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CrossingCountAffine.lean#L96-L99","doc":"**The second difference kills every affine function.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.secondDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.secondDiff","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CrossingCountAffine.lean#L92-L94","doc":"The second difference of `f` at `Z`. It annihilates affine functions and\ndetects a quadratic's leading coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.strong_channel_carries_charge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.strong_channel_carries_charge","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CrossingCountAffine.lean#L84-L88","doc":"The **strong** (symmetric) channel multiplicity, `(n₊ - n₋)/2 = 2Z`, stated\nas `n₊ - n₋ = 4Z`. All of the charge dependence sits here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.coulomb_channel_charge_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.coulomb_channel_charge_free","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CrossingCountAffine.lean#L77-L82","doc":"The **Coulomb** (antisymmetric) channel multiplicity, `(n₊ + n₋)/2`, stated\nwithout the division as the identity `n₊ + n₋ = 2(5A - 1)`. It depends on `A`\nalone — this is the mirror-blindness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.nMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.nMinus","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CrossingCountAffine.lean#L74-L75","doc":"`n₋ = 5A - 1 - 2Z`, the negative-crossing count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.nPlus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CrossingCountAffine.nPlus","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CrossingCountAffine.lean#L70-L72","doc":"`n₊ = 5A - 1 + 2Z`, the positive-crossing count of the canonical atomic\nbraid, as measured. ","signatureChunk":0}]}